   "title": "Defense ministry conducting poll on military cadets over proposed academy integration",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/defense/20261113/defense-ministry-conducting-poll-on-military-cadets-over-proposed-academy-integration",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:57:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794549422.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "The defense ministry said Friday it is surveying military cadets on the proposal to integrate the Army, Air Force and Navy academies as the government seeks to revise the plan amid pushback from alumni groups and key stakeholders. The online survey, running from Friday through Tuesday, will poll 2,350 cadets across all four class years, excluding about 143 naval cadets set to be deployed for rotational training, a ministry official told reporters.",
   "summary_zh": "国防部周五表示，正在就合并陆军、空军和海军军校的提议对军事学员进行调查。此前，校友团体和主要利益相关方反对合并方案，政府因此寻求修改相关计划。该部官员告诉记者，这项在线调查从周五持续至周二，将调查四个年级共2,350名学员，但不包括约143名将接受轮换培训的海军学员。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The defense ministry said Friday it is surveying military cadets on the proposal to integrate the Army, Air Force and Navy academies as the government seeks to revise the plan amid pushback from alumni groups and key stakeholders. The online survey, running from Friday through Tuesday, will poll 2,350 cadets across all four class years, excluding about 143 naval cadets set to be deployed for rotational training, a ministry official told reporters. The ministry is pushing to merge the three institutions into a unified military academy, but the plan has drawn fierce opposition from cadets and alumni who say it could erode the distinct identity and specialized capabilities of each armed service. The ministry is now reportedly weighing the option of relocating the military academy of the Army out of Seoul as planned while retaining the two others, a move seen as backtracking from its original merger plan. \"The survey aims to evaluate the current military academies and collect cadets' opinions as part of broader efforts to gather input from various sectors to refine the plan for establishing a unified military academy,\" the official said. The questionnaire centers on how to strengthen educational capabilities, including facilities, faculty and curricula, while preserving the traditions and specialized expertise of each military branch. It also gauges cadet interest in a proposed graduate school program under the current integration plan and asks them to provide open-ended feedback on the ministry's plan to establish a unified military academy, the official added",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
