   "title": "Amit Shah reviews Delhi law and order for second time in a month",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Delhi/amit-shah-reviews-delhi-law-and-order-for-second-time-in-a-month/article71695081.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:09:24 +0530",
   "_dt": 1794548364.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Union Home Minister Amit Shah visited the Delhi Police headquarters on Jai Singh Marg in Central Delhi on Thursday (November 12, 2026) to review the law-and-order situation and policing in the national capital. Shah arrived at the headquarters at 3.15 p.m. and left around 7 p.m. The nearly four-hour-long meeting focused on the police force’s preparedness and the law-and-order situation in the Capital.",
   "summary_zh": "通过订阅解锁这些内容：内政部长Amit Shah于周四（2026年11月12日）前往位于德里市中心Jai Singh Marg的德里警察总部，考察全国首都的治安状况和警务工作。Shah于下午3时15分抵达总部，约晚上7时离开。这次近四小时的会议重点讨论了警方的应急准备情况以及首都的治安状况。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Union Home Minister Amit Shah visited the Delhi Police headquarters on Jai Singh Marg in Central Delhi on Thursday (November 12, 2026) to review the law-and-order situation and policing in the national capital. Delhi Lieutenant Governor Taranjit Singh Sandhu, Delhi Police Commissioner Anurag Kumar and other senior police officers were also present at the meeting. Shah arrived at the headquarters at 3.15 p.m. and left around 7 p.m. The nearly four-hour-long meeting focused on the police force’s preparedness and the law-and-order situation in the Capital. However, the details of the discussions were not shared with the media, and senior police officers remained tight-lipped about the meeting. Sources said officers had also been instructed not to disclose its contents. Less than a month ago, Mr. Shah had held a similar meeting with senior police officers, which was also attended by Chief Minister Rekha Gupta. During the previous meeting, Mr. Shah reviewed the police’s preparedness to handle large gatherings and protests, intelligence gathering, crowd management and coordination among various units. The discussions also covered women’s safety, drug trafficking, organised crime networks, traffic management and measures to prevent protests from escalating into law-and-order situations. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "in"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
